    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d187-a1">

                <pb facs="0372" n="276" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg276"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No. 35.]</seg></opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Powell to General Heureaux.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Santo Domingo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1898-03-05"><hi rendition="#italic">March 5,
                        1898</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 15.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have received by cable this
                    evening instructions from my Government informing me that it has named Mr.
                    Alfred Noble, engineer, to examine and finally determine value of Ozama Bridge
                    concession and franchise; his compensation and expenses to be borne by your
                    Government and claimant in equal proportions.</p>
                <p>You will kindly favor me, your excellency, in giving your assent to this
                    proposition.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">W. F. Powell.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
